---
import ProsePage from '../components/ProsePage.astro';
import { company } from '../data/company';
---

<ProsePage
  path="/privacy/"
  crumbLabel="Privacy"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  heading="Privacy policy"
  lead={`This SDF Clothing privacy policy explains what personal information ${company.legalName} collects through ${company.officialDomain}. It covers why we collect it, who handles it, how long we keep it and your choices.`}
>
  <h2>Who is responsible for your information</h2>
  <p>
    {company.legalName}, {company.address.street}, {company.address.locality} {company.address.postalCode}, {company.address.countryName}, is the controller of the
    personal information described here. Contact us about privacy through our <a href={company.contactPath}>contact form</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <h3>When you send a quote request</h3>
  <p>
    We collect the details you enter: your name, email address, brand or company, website, country, product details, quantities, target price, timeline, any
    file links and your message. We also record the date and time of the request.
  </p>
  <h3>When you browse the site</h3>
  <p>
    We use Cloudflare Web Analytics, which measures page views and performance without cookies and without identifying you. Our hosting provider,
    Cloudflare, processes your IP address for a short time to deliver the site securely and protect it from abuse.
  </p>
  <h3>Spam protection</h3>
  <p>
    The quote form uses Cloudflare Turnstile to check that a request comes from a person, and a rate limit that counts requests from the same IP address for one
    minute. Neither is used for advertising.
  </p>

  <h2>Why we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>To reply to your request</strong> and prepare a quote, based on the steps you asked us to take before a possible contract.</li>
    <li><strong>To run an order</strong> if you become a customer, to perform that contract.</li>
    <li><strong>To keep the site secure and working</strong>, based on our legitimate interest in protecting it.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell your information, use it for advertising profiles or send marketing email without your consent.</p>

  <h2>Who processes it for us</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Cloudflare, Inc.</strong> hosts the site, runs the form, analytics, spam protection and rate limiting.</li>
    <li><strong>Resend</strong> delivers the emails generated by the quote form to our team and the confirmation to you.</li>
    <li><strong>Our email provider</strong> stores the correspondence that follows.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    These providers may process data outside your country, including in the United States. Where the law requires it, transfers rely on safeguards such as
    standard contractual clauses.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    We keep quote requests that do not lead to an order for up to 24 months, so we can answer follow-up questions, then delete them. If you become a customer,
    we keep order records for as long as tax and company law requires.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You may have rights under laws such as the UK GDPR, the EU GDPR or your own country's privacy law. Depending on where you live, you can ask to access, correct or delete your
    information, object to or restrict its use, and receive a copy of it. Send your request through our <a href={company.contactPath}>contact form</a> and we will reply within
    one month. You can also complain to your local data protection authority.
  </p>

  <h2>Browser storage</h2>
  <p>
    The site sets no advertising or tracking cookies. The colour theme follows your device setting and nothing is stored. Read the
    <a href="/cookies/">cookie policy</a> for details.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>When we change this policy, we update the date at the top of this page. Significant changes are also noted on the page itself.</p>
</ProsePage>
